                "remarks": "Residual assessment gap: Verifies that macro security values live under the Policies hive and are GPO-delivered, which makes them read-only to a standard user. It does NOT prove a user cannot change them by other means: a local administrator, an MDM policy conflict, or a user with registry write access to the Policies key would still be able to, and none of that is visible from the value itself."
