                    "description": "Microsoft Office macros are disabled for human users that do not have a demonstrated business requirement."
                  }
                ],
                "remarks": "Residual assessment gap: Checks that VBAWarnings is set to 4 (disable all macros without notification) by policy. It CANNOT assess the \"demonstrated business requirement\" half of the control at all -- whether a user who has macros enabled is authorised is an organisational fact held outside the host. A pass here means macros are disabled, not that the exemption process is sound; a fail may be a legitimately approved exemption."
